			<div class="author-description">
			Emma Hall is a journalist and editorial consultant and is the former Europe Editor of Ad Age, where she covered  European marketing advertising, digital and media stories. She has written for newspapers including the Financial Times, The Guardian, The Times and the Telegraph, and was previously a section editor at Campaign. Emma started her career in New York as a researcher for a biography of Keith Richards.		</div><!-- #author-description -->
